C o m p i l a t i o n


   1  *Trying out simplest model for project
   2  *current sets: regions (US and RoW), aluminum type (primary or secondary)
   3  *will have to complicate regions sets to add more countries
   4  *will have to add time dimension, will also be a new set?
   5  *****NEXT STEPS: FIND ACCURATE DATA, ADD CANADA, ADD A SHOCK******
   6   
   7  set r /USA, ROW/;
   8  set al /primary, secondary/;
   9   
  10  *parameters = essentially cost curves, FIND BETTER NUMBERS - currently using rough estimated numbers from AI
  11  *prices USD/metric ton , qty = metric tons , currently total aluminum (primary + secondary)
  12  parameter
  13  ****NUMBERS ARE PRETTY RANDOM NEED TO SEARCH FOR BETTER DATA"
  14  *price of aluminum USA and ROW
  15  pbar(r,al) /USA.primary 2855, USA.secondary 100, ROW.primary 100, ROW.secondary 2420/,
  16  *qty supplied aluminum USA and ROW
  17  qbar_s(r,al) /USA.primary 2236000, USA.secondary 100, ROW.primary 96000000, ROW.secondary 100/,
  18  *qty demanded aluminum USA and ROW
  19  qbar_d(r,al) /USA.primary 5830000, USA.secondary 100, ROW.primary 92406000, ROW.secondary 100/,
  20  **should break out elasticities more or keep as just supply and demand generally?
  21  *elasticity of supply generally
  22  e_s /0.4/
  23  *elasticity of demand generally
  24  e_d /-0.4/;
  25   
  26  *currently based off of Pd = a + b*Qd, Ps = c + d*Qs, where a,b,c,d are parameters
  27  *will have to break out for primary and secondary aluminun and include the different elasticities for each country
  28  parameter a(r,al),b(r,al),c(r,al),d(r,al);
  29   
  30  *is this right?
  31  b(r,al) = pbar(r,al) / (e_d * qbar_d(r,al));
  32  a(r,al) = pbar(r,al) - b(r,al) * qbar_d(r,al);
  33  d(r,al) = pbar(r,al) / (e_s * qbar_s(r,al));
  34  c(r,al) = pbar(r,al) - d(r,al) * qbar_s(r,al);
  35   
  36  *t will essentially be the cost of transportation/logistics?
  37  parameter t(al) ;
  38  *!!! here you'll want to make sure that the prices for primary in ROW > USA, and vice versa for secondary
  39  t("primary") = pbar('ROW',"primary") - pbar('USA',"primary");
  40  t("secondary") = pbar('USA',"secondary") - pbar('ROW',"secondary");
  41   
  42   
  43  *varibales - will have to have more specefic to primary and secondary
  44  positive variable Qd(r,al), Qs(r,al);
  45  positive variable X(al) "exports";
  46  variable W "total welfare";
  47   
  48  *will have to have market clearing for different countries and primary/secondary once added
  49  *also will have to add different constrains ie EU restiricitions on secondary exports once 2027....
  50  equation objfn, market_clearing_USA, market_clearing_ROW;
  51   
  52   
  53  objfn.. W =e=
  54     sum((r,al), a(r,al) * Qd(r,al) + b(r,al) * Qd(r,al) *Qd(r,al) /2
  55     - c(r,al) * Qs(r,al) - d(r,al) *Qs(r,al) * Qs(r,al) / 2 )
  56     - sum(al, t(al) * X(al));
  57   
  58  market_clearing_USA(al).. Qd('USA',al) + X(al)$sameas(al,"primary") =e= Qs('USA',al) + X(al)$sameas(al,"secondary");
  59  market_clearing_ROW(al).. Qd('ROW',al) + X(al)$sameas(al,"secondary") =e= Qs('ROW',al) + X(al)$sameas(al,"primary");
  60   
  61  model simple /all/;
  62   
  63  solve simple using QCP maximizing W;
